The story of the workers in the vineyard (vineyards)
The kingdom of the heavens is like a man who was a householder, who went out early in the morning to hire laborers for his vineyard.
He agreed to pay them the usual wage for a day's work. Then he sent them into his vineyard.
Around 9 a.m., he went out again. He saw others standing in the market doing nothing.
He told them: "And you, go and help me in my vineyard, and I will pay you your rightful wage."
This is how they went. He went out again around noon and three hours and did the same thing.
Around five o'clock, he went out and found others still standing around him. He asked them, "Why do you stand here all day long without doing anything?"
