The crowd ordered them to stop. They told them to be silent. But the two men screamed even louder, "Lord! Son of David! Have mercy on us!"
Jesus stood up and called to them, "What do you want me to do for you?" he asked them.
"Sir," they replied, "we want to be able to see."
Jesus felt a deep concern for them. He touched their eyes. Immediately, they were able to see. And they followed him.
