The Wedding Dinner Story
Jesus said to them other stories. He said,
Here is how the Kingdom of Heaven is like. A king who prepared a wedding feast for his son.
He sold his servant to those he invited to dinner. The servant told them to come, but they refused.
Then he sent some of the servants again. And he said, "Tell the invited guests that I have prepared my supper. I have killed my fattened calves and my best sheep. Everything is ready. Come to the wedding supper."
But the people paid no attention. One went off to his field, another to his business.
The others arrested his servants. They treated them badly and then killed them.
The king turned away furiously. He sent his army to destroy them. Those murderers were killed, and their city was burned.
Then the king said to his servant, "The wedding dinner is ready. But those I invited were not fit to attend."
Go to the corners. Invite to dinner anyone you can find.
The servants went out into the streets. They gathered all the people they found, good and bad. Soon the wedding hall was filled with guests.
The king went in to see the guests. He noticed a man there who was not dressed in wedding attire.
"Friend," he asked, "how did you get in here without your wedding clothes?" The man couldn't think of anything to say.
Then the king said to his servant, "Bind his hands and feet. Throw him outside into the darkness. There people will wail and grind their teeth."
