e would have been on guard and would not have allowed his house to be broken into. So you also must be ready, for the Son of Man will come at an hour when you do not expect Him. Who then is the faithful and wise servant whom his master has put in charge of his household to give them food and water at the proper time? Blessed is that servant whom his master finds doing so when he comes. But I tell you, that servant who knows his master's will but does not get ready or do what his master wants him to do, will be punished severely, and when the master of that servant returns, he will find him dressed inappropriately and behaving unbecomingly, and he will say to him, 'You wicked servant! You knew that I expect those who serve me to be ready to give food to my household at the proper time. So why were you not on guard and ready, so that you could have given them what was needed at the appointed time? Therefore, you wicked servant, I will have you punished severely before I throw you out into the darkness, where there will be weeping and grinding of teeth.' And that is what the Son of Man will do to those unfaithful servants when he comes in his glory and is revealed in his presence, and he will execute his judgment upon them, and their wickedness will be repaid them, and they will receive the reward they deserve. But blessed are those servants whom their master finds watching over his household and ready to give food to his servants at the proper time. That servant you find doing this will be blessed, and you should say to him, 'Blessed are you, you servant of our Lord! Because you have been faithful in very small matters, be trusted with much more. Enter into the joy of your Lord!' And do not forget to do the same for the other servants you find ready and watching over their master
